description.narrative:
As part of the operationalization of the Senegal Emerging Plan (PSE), particularly in its pillar relating to the "structural transformation of the economy and growth", the Government of PSE wishes to implement the Agropole center for the transformation structure of the agricultural production system in order to contribute to a transfer of investments and human resources from agriculture to agro-industry.

Identified among the 27 flagship projects of the Senegal E as one of the decisive levers for achieving food sovereignty and progressing in industrialization, the Agropole center will contribute to:

- stimulate the structural transformation of the country's economy;
- contribute to sustainable and inclusive development mainly in rural areas;
- create a more conducive environment for increased investment and the generation of decent jobs in the agribusiness and related sectors;
- reduce the trade balance deficit by increasing exports and import substitution

The overall objective of the project is to contribute to the structural transformation of the Senegalese economy and the improvement of food security, through the development of agro-industry and the sustainable increase in the productivity of agro-industrial sectors. priorities.

